-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Crystal Kingdom Dizzy
  Publisher   Codemasters, 1992
  Version     1.1

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Dizzy VII - Crystal Kingdom Dizzy (1992)(Codemasters)[128K].z80
  MD5         0cb1cb260b2f17305ef41c30af0e1f8f

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Changes     1.1: Starts with the Next's DivMMC automap switched off:
              NextZXOS leaves it on, and on current cores that could crash the
              game or spoil its drawing

  Note        Keys: 1 on the options, 1 to start; Z left, X right, SPACE to
              jump, ENTER for the inventory. Dizzy and everything that moves
              are white Next sprites over their own pixels, so they no longer
              take the colour of the scenery they pass; the rooms, the panel
              and the windows stay as the game draws them. Where an item the
              game copies straight onto the screen meets Dizzy, Dizzy stays in
              front (the original drew the item over him). Known issue: the
              sprite updates add about 2 ms to each game update, so play is up
              to about 5% slower than the original (estimated from the hook
              cost, not measured).

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  Infinite energy

  Checked against this release's code: the DEC (HL) that takes a heart (60808)
  and the one that takes a life (57267) become NOPs. In a free run the hearts
  stay at 3 with the cheat (2 without); no life was lost in testing, so
  Infinite lives is checked from the code only. Not played.

