-- TESTING -------------------------------------------------------------------
  Tested      NexClash differential verification against four machine-played
              recordings; run from its menu in OverSpec with both cheats on;
              Tang FPGA board: loads and plays. Not played by a person.

  Replay      IDENTICAL on 4 machine-played recordings, 36,183 frames (walks
              through Tree Roots, Daisy's House, the Garden and the rooms the
              walks reached, with the inventory): at every hook original and
              patched code from the same state to a common resume point (every
              register but R, all memory), every masked object draw predicted
              from its data and checked against the game's own screen writes
              (38,886 draws), each object's sprites against that drawing at
              every restore pass (4.7 million sprite pixels), and no screen
              write under a shown sprite except the counted case of a plain-
              copy item over Dizzy; 840 unit cases (every draw routine, plain
              and mirrored, at every height and edge position) pass; 8 of 8
              negative controls detected

  Emulator    OverSpec, from the patch menu: Infinite lives and Infinite
              energy on, Tree Roots and Daisy's House reached

  Coverage    Machine-played walks only: the opening rooms and the inventory;
              most of the game, puzzles, deaths and the ending not reached

  Hardware    Tang Nano 20K FPGA build of the Next, with DivMMC automap on and
              124 sprites left visible by a previous program: loads, plays
              through Tree Roots, the Back Yard and Daisy's House, no crash

  Nothing here claims a result on real hardware unless the line above says so.

-- HOW TO USE ----------------------------------------------------------------
  Put this .nxc and the game file in the same folder on the Next's card and
  choose the .nxc in the Browser. See README.txt.
